Abstract = {A kernel in a digraph is an independent and absorbent subset of its
   vertex set. A digraph is critical kernel imperfect if it does not have a
   kernel, but every proper induced subdigraph does. In this article, we
   characterize asymmetrical 4-quasi-transitive and 4-transitive digraphs,
   as well as 2-anti-transitive, and asymmetrical 4-anti-transitive
   digraphs with bounded diameter, which are critical kernel imperfect. (c)
   2025 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier B.V. This is an open access
