Title = {Direct-photon production in in elastic and high-multiplicity
   proton-proton collisions at √s=13 TeV},
Journal = {PHYSICS LETTERS B},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {868},
Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {In this letter, we present the first measurement of direct photons at
   the transverse momentum of 1 < p(T) < 6 GeV/c at midrapidity in
   inelastic and high-multiplicity proton-proton collisions at a
   centre-of-mass energy of root s = 13 TeV. The fraction of virtual direct
   photons in the inclusive virtual photon spectrum is obtained from a fit
   to the dielectron invariant mass spectrum. In the limit of zero
   invariant mass, this fraction is equal to the relative contribution of
   real direct photons in the inclusive real photon spectrum. Contributions
   from decays of light-flavour neutral mesons are estimated using
   independent measurements in proton-proton collisions at the same energy
   and the same event class. For the first time at the LHC energies, a
   direct-photon signal is observed at low p(T) in both inelastic and
   high-multiplicity event classes, with a significance of 3.2 sigma and
   1.9 sigma in terms of standard deviations, correspondingly. The yield of
   direct photons in inelastic pp collisions is compared to perturbative
   QCD calculations. The integrated photon yield is studied as a function
   of charged-particle multiplicity and is compared to the results from
   other experiments and theoretical calculations. The results show a
   significant increase of direct-photon yield with charged-particle
   multiplicity.},
