Year = {2025},
Volume = {1321},
Number = {4},
Month = {FEB 5},
Abstract = {Structure and conformation of tert-butyl(4-ethynylphenyl)carbamate, the
   compound combining carbamate and alkyne parts within the molecule, were
   studied using single X-ray diffraction analysis, NMR, FTIR and UV-vis
   spectroscopies. For unambiguous assignment of the signals H-1 and
   C-13-APT-NMR, HMQC and HMBC-NMR experiments were realized. The compound
   crystallized in orthorhombic crystal system, displaying N-H-O hydrogen
   bonds and C-H-pi interactions. The X-ray structure has been recreated by
   means of theoretical calculations in order to assess the proposed
   arrangement and discuss the source of the intra and intermolecular
   relationships. The use of Grimme, Wiberg and Hirshfeld surface tools
   were applied to have a good confirmation of the presence and importance
   of hydrogen bonds.},
